{"id":"audit-on-file-return-says-none","title":"An audit on file, and a return that says none was required","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"Do returns that say no federal audit was required agree with the clearinghouse?","finding":"33 returns answer no, or leave the question blank, for a year in which the clearinghouse holds an audit of the same organization. The largest by federal spending in the audit: Bay Area Community Services (year ended 2023-06-30, $20.9 million); Bay Area Community Services (year ended 2024-06-30, $17.0 million); Conard House Inc (year ended 2024-06-30, $9.4 million); Conard House Inc (year ended 2023-06-30, $9.4 million).","how":"The same join as the screen before, the other way round: an audit on file for the employer number and year end, and Part XII line 3a answered no or left blank.","limits":"A voluntary audit, or one required by a state or City funder at a lower threshold, can explain an audit on file alongside a no answer. A blank answer leaves the filer’s position unclear. For the fiscal years covered here, the federal audit threshold depends on the start of the entity’s fiscal year. It was $750,000 in federal awards expended across all programs for years starting before October 1, 2024, and $1 million for years starting on or after that date. An entity reaches the threshold at either amount. City payments alone cannot establish how much federal funding the recipient expended.","columns":[{"k":"org","t":"Organization","type":"org"},{"k":"yearEnd","t":"Year ended","type":"date"},{"k":"answer","t":"Return says audit required","type":"text"},{"k":"federalSpent","t":"Federal money spent, per the audit","type":"usd"},{"k":"accepted","t":"Audit accepted","type":"date"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City paid that year","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"org":"Bay Area Community Services","orgKey":"BAY AREA COMMUNITY SERVICES","yearEnd":"2023-06-30","answer":"No","federalSpent":20853373,"auditType":"single audit","accepted":"2024-10-01","cityPaid":469199},{"org